1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,629
May 2022.

2
00:00:00,629 --> 00:00:06,501
In just a few days, a cryptocurrency worth
around 40 billion dollars falls to almost

3
00:00:06,501 --> 00:00:06,850
zero.

4
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:12,652
Its price had been above 100 dollars only
a month earlier. Now it's worth less than

5
00:00:12,652 --> 00:00:13,141
a cent.

6
00:00:13,691 --> 00:00:18,339
In apartments across Seoul, in Singapore,
in the United States, hundreds of

7
00:00:18,339 --> 00:00:22,243
thousands of people watch their savings
disappear in real time.

8
00:00:22,243 --> 00:00:25,466
Many of them had been told this was the
safe option.

9
00:00:26,466 --> 00:00:29,602
The man behind it had once mocked his
critics online.

10
00:00:29,602 --> 00:00:34,040
A year later, he would be arrested at an
airport in the Balkans with a fake

11
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:34,573
passport.

12
00:00:34,823 --> 00:00:39,988
And years after that, standing in a New
York courtroom, he would finally admit

13
00:00:39,988 --> 00:00:43,762
what really happened the first time his
coin nearly died.

14
00:00:43,762 --> 00:00:45,881
This is the story of Terra-Luna.

15
00:00:47,381 --> 00:00:53,245
Do Kwon grew up in Seoul, studied computer
science at Stanford, and worked briefly as

16
00:00:53,245 --> 00:00:56,211
a software engineer at Microsoft and
Apple.

17
00:00:56,211 --> 00:01:01,937
Then he came home. In 2016, he started a
small wireless networking company in Korea

18
00:01:01,937 --> 00:01:02,834
called Anyfi.

19
00:01:03,084 --> 00:01:06,372
It was a modest startup. What came next
was not.

20
00:01:06,922 --> 00:01:12,896
In early 2018, Kwon co-founded Terraform
Labs with Daniel Shin, one of Korea's

21
00:01:12,896 --> 00:01:15,041
best-known startup founders.

22
00:01:15,041 --> 00:01:20,785
Shin had built Ticket Monster, or TMON,
one of the country's big e-commerce

23
00:01:20,785 --> 00:01:24,462
platforms, and he knew merchants all over
Korea.

24
00:01:24,712 --> 00:01:28,575
The pairing made sense. Kwon had the code.
Shin had the customers.

25
00:01:29,125 --> 00:01:34,674
Kwon also had something else: a voice. On
Twitter, he was sharp, funny, and

26
00:01:34,674 --> 00:01:36,597
supremely sure of himself.

27
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:42,516
By 2022, around a million people followed
him. To many of them, he wasn't just a

28
00:01:42,516 --> 00:01:44,513
founder. He was the future.

29
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:47,983
Terra's big idea was a stablecoin.

30
00:01:47,983 --> 00:01:54,854
Most cryptocurrencies swing wildly in
price. A stablecoin is supposed to stay at

31
00:01:54,854 --> 00:01:56,485
one dollar. Always.

32
00:01:56,485 --> 00:02:01,810
That stability is what lets people use
crypto like real money.

33
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:07,465
Most stablecoins do this the boring way.
For every coin, they hold a real dollar,

34
00:02:07,465 --> 00:02:09,545
or something like it, in reserve.

35
00:02:09,545 --> 00:02:10,364
Terra didn't.

36
00:02:11,564 --> 00:02:15,762
But before we look at how Terra worked,
you need to see how it was sold.

37
00:02:15,762 --> 00:02:20,544
Because in the beginning, the pitch wasn't
about getting rich. It was about buying

38
00:02:20,544 --> 00:02:20,952
coffee.

39
00:02:21,502 --> 00:02:26,985
In 2019, Shin's other company launched a
mobile payments app in Korea called Chai.

40
00:02:26,985 --> 00:02:31,866
Shoppers got discounts. Merchants paid
lower fees than the card companies

41
00:02:31,866 --> 00:02:32,401
charged.

42
00:02:32,651 --> 00:02:37,721
And Terra told the world that, behind the
scenes, those payments were running on the

43
00:02:37,721 --> 00:02:38,747
Terra blockchain.

44
00:02:39,297 --> 00:02:44,884
Terra didn't only have a dollar coin. It
also had a coin pegged to the Korean won,

45
00:02:44,884 --> 00:02:45,634
called KRT.

46
00:02:45,884 --> 00:02:51,906
In 2019, Chai partnered with Terraform to
bring that won coin into its app. Every

47
00:02:51,906 --> 00:02:57,854
coffee, every online order, was supposed
to be a tiny proof that Terra worked as

48
00:02:57,854 --> 00:02:58,300
money.

49
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:03,782
Terra's own announcements boasted of
hundreds of thousands of users and

50
00:03:03,782 --> 00:03:05,518
millions of transactions.

51
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:08,575
For investors, this was the killer
argument.

52
00:03:08,575 --> 00:03:14,062
Most crypto projects were just promises.
Terra could point to real people, in a

53
00:03:14,062 --> 00:03:16,632
real country, paying for real things.

54
00:03:17,632 --> 00:03:22,460
Keep the name Chai in mind. It comes back
later in this story. In a courtroom.

55
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,113
Terra had two coins.

56
00:03:25,113 --> 00:03:28,600
UST, the stablecoin meant to stay at one
dollar.

57
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:32,887
And LUNA, its sister coin, whose price
could rise and fall.

58
00:03:33,437 --> 00:03:38,561
The system promised that you could always
swap one UST for one dollar's worth of

59
00:03:38,561 --> 00:03:39,522
LUNA, and back.

60
00:03:39,522 --> 00:03:44,582
If UST dropped below a dollar, traders
could buy it cheap, swap it for a dollar

61
00:03:44,582 --> 00:03:46,824
of LUNA, and pocket the difference.

62
00:03:47,074 --> 00:03:51,253
In theory, that buying pressure would push
UST back to a dollar. Forever.

63
00:03:51,803 --> 00:03:53,917
Here's what that looks like.

64
00:03:53,917 --> 00:04:00,032
Say UST slips to 97 cents. You buy one.
You hand it to the system, which destroys

65
00:04:00,032 --> 00:04:06,072
it, and gives you one dollar's worth of
brand-new LUNA. You've made three cents.

66
00:04:06,322 --> 00:04:12,249
Thousands of traders doing that at once
remove UST from circulation, until the

67
00:04:12,249 --> 00:04:14,528
price climbs back to a dollar.

68
00:04:14,528 --> 00:04:20,835
And if UST goes above a dollar, it works
the other way: burn LUNA, create UST, sell

69
00:04:20,835 --> 00:04:21,063
it.

70
00:04:22,063 --> 00:04:26,095
There was no vault of dollars behind it.
Just code, and confidence.

71
00:04:26,095 --> 00:04:30,487
And the whole thing depended on one
assumption: that LUNA would always be

72
00:04:30,487 --> 00:04:31,450
worth something.

73
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,555
Critics called it what it looked like: a
design that could spiral to zero if

74
00:04:36,555 --> 00:04:37,874
confidence ever broke.

75
00:04:37,874 --> 00:04:41,230
Kwon's response to critics was famous for
its arrogance.

76
00:04:41,230 --> 00:04:45,966
When one of them challenged him online, he
replied: "I don't debate the poor on

77
00:04:45,966 --> 00:04:46,505
Twitter."

78
00:04:47,705 --> 00:04:49,085
Then came the bait.

79
00:04:49,085 --> 00:04:54,748
A lending platform built on Terra, called
Anchor Protocol, offered close to 20

80
00:04:54,748 --> 00:04:57,653
percent annual interest on UST deposits.

81
00:04:57,903 --> 00:05:02,781
Your bank was offering almost nothing.
Anchor offered nearly 20 percent, on a

82
00:05:02,781 --> 00:05:06,012
coin that was supposed to be as stable as
a dollar.

83
00:05:06,562 --> 00:05:07,880
Money poured in.

84
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:14,389
By early 2022, the vast majority of all
UST in existence was sitting in Anchor,

85
00:05:14,389 --> 00:05:15,954
earning that yield.

86
00:05:15,954 --> 00:05:22,051
LUNA's price soared above 100 dollars.
Terra's total value reached tens of

87
00:05:22,051 --> 00:05:23,699
billions of dollars.

88
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:29,297
Terraform even signed a five-year
sponsorship deal with the Washington

89
00:05:29,297 --> 00:05:34,034
Nationals baseball team, reported at about
38 million dollars.

90
00:05:34,034 --> 00:05:39,536
In Korea, Kwon was hailed as a crypto
genius. His fans called themselves

91
00:05:39,536 --> 00:05:40,376
"Lunatics."

92
00:05:41,376 --> 00:05:44,904
But where was that 20 percent actually
coming from?

93
00:05:44,904 --> 00:05:50,577
For a long time, the honest answer was:
largely from Terra itself, subsidizing the

94
00:05:50,577 --> 00:05:52,445
payments to keep people in.

95
00:05:52,995 --> 00:05:57,791
Anchor kept a reserve to cover the gap
between what borrowers paid and what

96
00:05:57,791 --> 00:05:59,389
depositors were promised.

97
00:05:59,389 --> 00:06:04,377
By early 2022, that reserve was draining
by more than a million dollars a day.

98
00:06:04,627 --> 00:06:11,065
So in February 2022, the Luna Foundation
Guard, an organization we'll meet properly

99
00:06:11,065 --> 00:06:16,959
in a minute, approved a top-up of 450
million dollars' worth of UST, just to

100
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:18,976
keep the 20 percent going.

101
00:06:19,226 --> 00:06:23,838
Shortly after, Anchor's community voted to
let the rate slowly come down. But by

102
00:06:23,838 --> 00:06:26,374
then, the promise had already done its
work.

103
00:06:27,574 --> 00:06:32,040
Here's the twist most people never heard
at the time.

104
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:38,022
In May 2021, a year before the final
collapse, UST had already lost its

105
00:06:38,022 --> 00:06:39,286
one-dollar peg.

106
00:06:39,286 --> 00:06:42,403
And then, mysteriously, it recovered.

107
00:06:42,953 --> 00:06:46,876
The public story was that the code worked.
The algorithm fixed itself.

108
00:06:46,876 --> 00:06:50,015
But years later, U.S. regulators told a
different story.

109
00:06:50,265 --> 00:06:55,827
According to the SEC, the recovery was
driven by a large trading firm quietly

110
00:06:55,827 --> 00:07:00,523
buying UST behind the scenes, under a
secret deal with Terraform.

111
00:07:01,073 --> 00:07:07,219
The SEC's account goes like this. On May
23, 2021, as UST slid, Terraform made a

112
00:07:07,219 --> 00:07:09,600
verbal agreement with the firm.

113
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:15,439
Terraform would loosen the restrictions on
the firm's right to buy LUNA at a

114
00:07:15,439 --> 00:07:16,130
discount.

115
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:22,660
In return, according to the SEC, the firm
bought more than 20 million dollars of UST

116
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,604
to push the price back up.

117
00:07:24,604 --> 00:07:30,735
The SEC said that investors were misled
into believing the algorithm had saved the

118
00:07:30,735 --> 00:07:31,034
peg.

119
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:36,604
The trading firm's affiliate later settled
with the SEC without admitting or denying

120
00:07:36,604 --> 00:07:37,301
the claims.

121
00:07:38,301 --> 00:07:44,569
If that's true, the system hadn't passed
its stress test. It had been rescued. And

122
00:07:44,569 --> 00:07:46,250
the rescue was hidden.

123
00:07:46,250 --> 00:07:51,601
So who knew? And would anyone ever admit
it? Hold on to that question.

124
00:07:52,801 --> 00:07:59,074
By early 2022, the warnings were getting
louder. Kwon's answer was a war chest.

125
00:07:59,074 --> 00:08:05,029
In January 2022, a nonprofit called the
Luna Foundation Guard was set up in

126
00:08:05,029 --> 00:08:05,823
Singapore.

127
00:08:05,823 --> 00:08:11,778
Its job was to build a reserve that could
defend UST's peg in an emergency.

128
00:08:12,028 --> 00:08:16,057
Kwon said the goal was 10 billion dollars'
worth of bitcoin.

129
00:08:16,607 --> 00:08:21,891
The first big chunk of money came in
February: a one-billion-dollar sale of

130
00:08:21,891 --> 00:08:27,808
LUNA to investors, led by two heavyweight
crypto firms, Jump Crypto and a hedge fund

131
00:08:27,808 --> 00:08:29,781
called Three Arrows Capital.

132
00:08:29,781 --> 00:08:32,951
Remember that second name. It comes back
too.

133
00:08:33,501 --> 00:08:38,620
And it bought fast. On some days that
spring, it was buying more than 100

134
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:41,215
million dollars of bitcoin at a time.

135
00:08:41,215 --> 00:08:46,614
Kwon said he expected to reach the
10-billion-dollar target by the end of the

136
00:08:46,614 --> 00:08:47,596
third quarter.

137
00:08:47,846 --> 00:08:54,381
Anyone could watch the reserve wallets
fill up on the blockchain, in real time.

138
00:08:54,381 --> 00:09:00,833
By early May, it held 80,394 bitcoin,
worth around 2.4 billion dollars. It had

139
00:09:00,833 --> 00:09:05,383
become one of the biggest bitcoin holders
in the world.

140
00:09:05,633 --> 00:09:12,130
To many investors, this looked like the
missing piece. The vault Terra never had,

141
00:09:12,130 --> 00:09:13,814
finally being filled.

142
00:09:14,814 --> 00:09:16,357
But there was a catch.

143
00:09:16,357 --> 00:09:22,110
The reserve was a fraction of the nearly
19 billion dollars of UST in circulation.

144
00:09:22,110 --> 00:09:27,792
And it was held in bitcoin, an asset that
could fall at exactly the moment it was

145
00:09:27,792 --> 00:09:28,283
needed.

146
00:09:28,533 --> 00:09:33,517
U.S. prosecutors later said there was
another problem: Kwon presented the

147
00:09:33,517 --> 00:09:38,705
foundation as independent from Terraform,
when, according to prosecutors, he

148
00:09:38,705 --> 00:09:39,661
controlled it.

149
00:09:40,211 --> 00:09:45,041
So before we watch the fall, here are two
questions to carry with you.

150
00:09:45,041 --> 00:09:50,423
Was the 2021 rescue really hidden from
investors? And were those Chai payments

151
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:52,079
really running on Terra?

152
00:09:52,329 --> 00:09:57,528
Both get answered before the end of this
video. One by a jury. The other by Do Kwon

153
00:09:57,528 --> 00:09:58,029
himself.

154
00:09:59,229 --> 00:10:00,917
Saturday, May 7, 2022.

155
00:10:00,917 --> 00:10:05,289
Anchor is holding about 14 billion
dollars' worth of UST.

156
00:10:05,289 --> 00:10:11,733
Terraform pulls a large amount of UST out
of a key trading pool on a platform called

157
00:10:11,733 --> 00:10:15,338
Curve, as part of a planned move to a new
pool.

158
00:10:15,588 --> 00:10:22,458
Within minutes, other wallets dump tens of
millions of UST into what's left.

159
00:10:22,458 --> 00:10:25,894
The pool tilts. UST slips to 99 cents.

160
00:10:25,894 --> 00:10:33,487
It sounds tiny. It isn't. For a coin whose
whole promise is one dollar, a penny is a

161
00:10:33,487 --> 00:10:35,205
crack in the glass.

162
00:10:35,755 --> 00:10:42,347
Sunday. Anchor depositors head for the
exit. Billions of dollars of UST leave in

163
00:10:42,347 --> 00:10:43,748
a matter of days.

164
00:10:43,748 --> 00:10:50,340
The Luna Foundation Guard says it will
lend 1.5 billion dollars, half in bitcoin

165
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:53,224
and half in UST, to defend the peg.

166
00:10:53,474 --> 00:10:57,421
Kwon tweets: "Deploying more capital.
Steady lads."

167
00:10:57,971 --> 00:11:00,694
Monday. The defense isn't working.

168
00:11:00,694 --> 00:11:06,940
The foundation's bitcoin starts leaving
its wallets to be sold. Bitcoin itself

169
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:09,263
slides toward 30,000 dollars.

170
00:11:09,263 --> 00:11:15,749
Anchor deposits fall from 14 billion to
under 9 billion. UST, at one point, drops

171
00:11:15,749 --> 00:11:17,271
to around 35 cents.

172
00:11:17,821 --> 00:11:20,826
And now the magic trick runs in reverse.

173
00:11:20,826 --> 00:11:25,108
To defend the peg, the system creates more
and more LUNA.

174
00:11:25,108 --> 00:11:31,343
More LUNA means each LUNA is worth less.
Which means less trust in UST. Which means

175
00:11:31,343 --> 00:11:32,320
more selling.

176
00:11:32,870 --> 00:11:38,094
Tuesday and Wednesday. Exchanges choke on
the flood of transactions. The world's

177
00:11:38,094 --> 00:11:42,469
largest exchange, Binance, briefly pauses
LUNA and UST withdrawals.

178
00:11:42,469 --> 00:11:47,693
LUNA, worth around 80 dollars at the start
of the month, falls below one dollar.

179
00:11:48,243 --> 00:11:53,456
The supply of LUNA explodes from hundreds
of millions of coins into the trillions.

180
00:11:54,006 --> 00:11:59,403
Thursday. The Terra blockchain itself is
halted. By Friday, it has been halted

181
00:11:59,403 --> 00:11:59,818
again.

182
00:11:59,818 --> 00:12:05,423
Major exchanges pull LUNA and UST from
trading. LUNA is now worth a tiny fraction

183
00:12:05,423 --> 00:12:06,115
of a cent.

184
00:12:06,365 --> 00:12:10,958
That Friday, Kwon writes: "I am
heartbroken about the pain my invention

185
00:12:10,958 --> 00:12:12,704
has brought on all of you."

186
00:12:13,254 --> 00:12:19,984
The following Monday, the Luna Foundation
Guard says it has 313 bitcoin left. Out of

187
00:12:19,984 --> 00:12:20,545
80,394.

188
00:12:20,545 --> 00:12:27,356
An audit the foundation released later put
the total spent defending the peg at about

189
00:12:27,356 --> 00:12:28,958
2.8 billion dollars.

190
00:12:29,958 --> 00:12:34,739
Around 40 billion dollars of value, gone
in a matter of days.

191
00:12:34,739 --> 00:12:40,148
Some victims had put in their life
savings. Many had trusted the word

192
00:12:40,148 --> 00:12:40,853
"stable."

193
00:12:42,053 --> 00:12:43,736
Who were the Lunatics?

194
00:12:43,736 --> 00:12:49,474
In Korea, they gathered in group chat
rooms and online forums. Overseas, on

195
00:12:49,474 --> 00:12:51,616
Reddit, Discord and Twitter.

196
00:12:51,616 --> 00:12:57,889
For two years, they shared memes, price
targets, and a kind of belonging. Kwon was

197
00:12:57,889 --> 00:12:58,960
their captain.

198
00:12:59,510 --> 00:13:01,396
Many of them weren't gamblers.

199
00:13:01,396 --> 00:13:06,551
The stories posted online came from office
workers, retirees, young couples saving

200
00:13:06,551 --> 00:13:11,770
for a home, people who had moved money out
of a bank because Anchor paid many times

201
00:13:11,770 --> 00:13:12,084
more.

202
00:13:12,634 --> 00:13:17,649
After the crash, those same communities
changed overnight. The memes stopped.

203
00:13:17,649 --> 00:13:23,184
Moderators of the biggest English-language
forum pinned links to support helplines at

204
00:13:23,184 --> 00:13:24,487
the top of the page.

205
00:13:24,737 --> 00:13:29,822
In Korea, where LUNA had traded on the
country's biggest exchanges, those

206
00:13:29,822 --> 00:13:31,842
exchanges moved to delist it.

207
00:13:31,842 --> 00:13:37,484
Groups of Korean investors filed criminal
complaints and lawsuits against Terra's

208
00:13:37,484 --> 00:13:38,111
founders.

209
00:13:39,111 --> 00:13:44,373
We are not naming any of them here. Their
losses are not entertainment.

210
00:13:44,373 --> 00:13:49,634
But every number in this story was
somebody's rent, somebody's savings,

211
00:13:49,634 --> 00:13:50,820
somebody's plan.

212
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:53,955
Terra did not fall alone.

213
00:13:53,955 --> 00:13:59,606
Remember Three Arrows Capital, the
Singapore-based hedge fund that helped

214
00:13:59,606 --> 00:14:06,030
lead that billion-dollar LUNA sale? It had
made a large bet on LUNA. When LUNA went

215
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:07,888
to zero, so did the bet.

216
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:12,577
By the start of July, a court in the
British Virgin Islands had ordered the

217
00:14:12,577 --> 00:14:13,524
fund liquidated.

218
00:14:14,074 --> 00:14:16,891
The firms that had lent to it were next.

219
00:14:16,891 --> 00:14:22,314
Voyager Digital, which said Three Arrows
had defaulted on a loan of about 650

220
00:14:22,314 --> 00:14:25,695
million dollars, filed for bankruptcy on
July 5.

221
00:14:25,945 --> 00:14:31,158
Celsius Network, a crypto lender that had
promised its users high yields, froze

222
00:14:31,158 --> 00:14:34,854
withdrawals in June and filed for
bankruptcy on July 13.

223
00:14:35,404 --> 00:14:37,351
And then there was FTX.

224
00:14:37,601 --> 00:14:42,808
At the criminal trial of FTX founder Sam
Bankman-Fried, a former top executive of

225
00:14:42,808 --> 00:14:47,630
his trading firm, Alameda Research,
testified that after the crash, lenders

226
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:52,966
started demanding their money back in June
2022, and that Alameda repaid them using

227
00:14:52,966 --> 00:14:55,216
money that came from FTX customers.

228
00:14:55,466 --> 00:15:01,077
FTX collapsed in November 2022.
Bankman-Fried was convicted of fraud a

229
00:15:01,077 --> 00:15:01,959
year later.

230
00:15:02,959 --> 00:15:07,482
Terra didn't commit FTX's fraud. A jury
put that on Bankman-Fried.

231
00:15:07,482 --> 00:15:13,239
But according to that testimony, the panic
that began in May was part of what pushed

232
00:15:13,239 --> 00:15:15,226
customer money into the hole.

233
00:15:16,426 --> 00:15:20,897
While the dominoes fell, Kwon proposed a
fix: start over.

234
00:15:20,897 --> 00:15:27,251
On May 25, Terra's community voted for a
new blockchain. On May 28, it went live.

235
00:15:27,501 --> 00:15:33,453
The new coin was also called LUNA. The old
chain was renamed Terra Classic, and the

236
00:15:33,453 --> 00:15:36,250
old coins became LUNA Classic and USTC.

237
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:42,932
Holders of the old coins received airdrops
of new LUNA, based on what they held and

238
00:15:42,932 --> 00:15:43,301
when.

239
00:15:43,301 --> 00:15:48,768
One thing was missing. There was no new
UST. Terra 2.0 launched without an

240
00:15:48,768 --> 00:15:50,984
algorithmic stablecoin at all.

241
00:15:51,234 --> 00:15:56,020
The new LUNA briefly traded above 17
dollars, then quickly fell as people sold

242
00:15:56,020 --> 00:15:57,432
what they'd been given.

243
00:15:57,432 --> 00:16:01,175
For many old holders, it was nowhere near
what they had lost.

244
00:16:02,375 --> 00:16:06,351
When the collapse hit, Kwon was living in
Singapore.

245
00:16:06,351 --> 00:16:12,315
In September 2022, a Seoul court issued a
warrant for his arrest, and Interpol

246
00:16:12,315 --> 00:16:13,844
issued a red notice.

247
00:16:13,844 --> 00:16:19,120
He said he wasn't on the run. But nobody
seemed to know where he was.

248
00:16:19,370 --> 00:16:24,649
Days after the warrant, Singapore police
said he was no longer in Singapore.

249
00:16:24,649 --> 00:16:30,067
In October, Korea's foreign ministry
invalidated his passport. Online, he kept

250
00:16:30,067 --> 00:16:32,429
posting as if nothing had changed.

251
00:16:32,979 --> 00:16:37,500
In March 2023, at the airport in
Podgorica, the capital of Montenegro,

252
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:40,987
police stopped a man trying to board a
private flight.

253
00:16:40,987 --> 00:16:43,958
He was carrying a forged Costa Rican
passport.

254
00:16:43,958 --> 00:16:44,927
It was Do Kwon.

255
00:16:45,177 --> 00:16:49,834
A Montenegrin court sentenced him to four
months in prison for the forged documents.

256
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:53,499
Both South Korea and the United States
wanted him.

257
00:16:53,499 --> 00:16:57,922
For more than a year and a half,
Montenegro's courts and ministers went

258
00:16:57,922 --> 00:17:01,349
back and forth over which country should
get him first.

259
00:17:01,349 --> 00:17:06,084
In the end, he was extradited to the
United States, on the last day of 2024.

260
00:17:07,284 --> 00:17:13,783
America went after Kwon twice. Once in
civil court. Once in criminal court.

261
00:17:14,333 --> 00:17:17,165
The SEC sued Terraform and Kwon in
February 2023.

262
00:17:17,165 --> 00:17:21,905
Remember Chai? The SEC alleged that Chai's
payments were not actually processed on

263
00:17:21,905 --> 00:17:26,125
the Terra blockchain, and that
transactions were copied onto the chain to

264
00:17:26,125 --> 00:17:27,801
make it look as if they were.

265
00:17:28,051 --> 00:17:33,034
In April 2024, a jury in New York found
Terraform and Kwon liable for fraud.

266
00:17:33,034 --> 00:17:38,345
Afterwards, the SEC said the trial had
exposed the defendants' lies about the use

267
00:17:38,345 --> 00:17:41,426
of the Terra blockchain to settle
transactions.

268
00:17:41,676 --> 00:17:48,213
In June 2024, Terraform and Kwon agreed to
a settlement of about 4.47 billion

269
00:17:48,213 --> 00:17:51,863
dollars, and Terraform agreed to wind
down.

270
00:17:52,413 --> 00:17:59,411
Then came the criminal case. In August
2025, Kwon pleaded guilty to two fraud

271
00:17:59,411 --> 00:18:02,683
charges. And in court, he said this:

272
00:18:02,683 --> 00:18:09,499
"In 2021, I made false and misleading
statements about why UST regained its

273
00:18:09,499 --> 00:18:09,953
peg."

274
00:18:10,953 --> 00:18:15,774
That was the hidden rescue. The question
from earlier, answered by the man himself.

275
00:18:16,324 --> 00:18:21,938
In December 2025, the judge sentenced him
to 15 years in prison. That was longer

276
00:18:21,938 --> 00:18:25,026
than the 12 years prosecutors had asked
for.

277
00:18:25,026 --> 00:18:29,307
The judge called it a fraud on an "epic,
generational scale."

278
00:18:30,507 --> 00:18:35,925
Most English coverage stops there. But the
biggest group of retail victims was in

279
00:18:35,925 --> 00:18:36,326
Korea.

280
00:18:36,326 --> 00:18:42,012
According to figures from Korean financial
authorities, about 280,000 people in Korea

281
00:18:42,012 --> 00:18:43,885
held LUNA when it collapsed.

282
00:18:44,135 --> 00:18:48,694
Within days of the crash, Seoul
prosecutors revived a financial-crimes

283
00:18:48,694 --> 00:18:54,165
unit nicknamed the "Yeouido Grim Reaper,"
after the district where Korea's financial

284
00:18:54,165 --> 00:18:57,356
industry lives. Terra was one of its first
cases.

285
00:18:57,906 --> 00:19:03,216
In April 2023, Korean prosecutors indicted
Daniel Shin and several others.

286
00:19:03,216 --> 00:19:09,172
Prosecutors allege that Chai made ordinary
payments look as if they were running on

287
00:19:09,172 --> 00:19:09,603
Terra.

288
00:19:09,853 --> 00:19:15,243
Shin denies wrongdoing. His lawyers say he
left Terra two years before the collapse

289
00:19:15,243 --> 00:19:17,192
and had nothing to do with it.

290
00:19:17,192 --> 00:19:22,257
Korean courts twice turned down requests
to arrest him, and his trial is still

291
00:19:22,257 --> 00:19:22,842
going on.

292
00:19:23,392 --> 00:19:26,470
And Do Kwon may not be done with Korean
justice.

293
00:19:26,470 --> 00:19:31,537
U.S. prosecutors said they would not
oppose a transfer to Korea after he serves

294
00:19:31,537 --> 00:19:32,691
half his sentence.

295
00:19:32,941 --> 00:19:37,769
In Korea, he would still face separate
charges, including under the capital

296
00:19:37,769 --> 00:19:42,532
markets law. Some Korean media have
reported that a conviction there could

297
00:19:42,532 --> 00:19:44,077
mean more than 30 years.

298
00:19:45,277 --> 00:19:49,119
Terra wasn't the first algorithmic
stablecoin to break.

299
00:19:49,119 --> 00:19:54,010
In June 2021, a project called Iron
Finance saw its partly algorithmic

300
00:19:54,010 --> 00:19:59,459
stablecoin lose its peg, while its sister
token fell from around 60 dollars to

301
00:19:59,459 --> 00:20:01,625
almost zero in less than a day.

302
00:20:01,875 --> 00:20:06,223
Same design idea. Same spiral. Smaller
scale.

303
00:20:06,773 --> 00:20:09,452
So why does the idea keep coming back?

304
00:20:09,452 --> 00:20:15,232
Because the dream is powerful. Money as
steady as a dollar, without anyone needing

305
00:20:15,232 --> 00:20:16,642
to hold the dollars.

306
00:20:16,892 --> 00:20:21,675
And because the mechanism works perfectly,
right up until the moment people stop

307
00:20:21,675 --> 00:20:24,426
believing in it. Confidence is the
collateral.

308
00:20:24,976 --> 00:20:30,364
And the yield makes the math look like
magic. Run the numbers yourself.

309
00:20:30,364 --> 00:20:36,208
Fourteen billion dollars of deposits, at
nearly 20 percent, means roughly 2.7

310
00:20:36,208 --> 00:20:39,547
billion dollars a year in promised
interest.

311
00:20:39,797 --> 00:20:45,341
Anchor's borrowers never paid anything
close to that. The difference had to come

312
00:20:45,341 --> 00:20:49,569
from somewhere: reserves, subsidies, and
new money coming in.

313
00:20:50,119 --> 00:20:55,992
Lawmakers noticed. In July 2025, the
United States passed the GENIUS Act, which

314
00:20:55,992 --> 00:21:01,865
requires payment stablecoins to be backed
one-for-one by reserves like cash and

315
00:21:01,865 --> 00:21:03,501
short-term Treasuries.

316
00:21:04,501 --> 00:21:07,655
This isn't investment advice. It's a
pattern.

317
00:21:07,655 --> 00:21:12,911
When a yield is far above what anything
safe pays, the money is coming from

318
00:21:12,911 --> 00:21:17,327
somewhere. If you can't see where, it
might be coming from you.

319
00:21:18,527 --> 00:21:21,377
Terra didn't fail because nobody warned it
would.

320
00:21:21,377 --> 00:21:25,914
It failed because a 20 percent promise was
more convincing than every warning.

321
00:21:26,914 --> 00:21:32,557
If something promises you high returns
with no risk, ask one question: where is

322
00:21:32,557 --> 00:21:34,771
the money actually coming from?

323
00:21:35,321 --> 00:21:38,820
Terra was a Korean story the whole world
watched.

324
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:44,677
Next time: a Korean story the world never
heard. A man who took money from tens of

325
00:21:44,677 --> 00:21:50,247
thousands of people, fled the country, and
was then reported dead. Many of his

326
00:21:50,247 --> 00:21:52,461
victims still don't believe it.

327
00:21:53,011 --> 00:21:54,986
Subscribe so you don't miss it.

328
00:21:54,986 --> 00:22:00,020
And tell me in the comments: did you, or
someone you know, ever get caught in a

329
00:22:00,020 --> 00:22:01,040
crypto collapse?

